TITLE:: REOfflineClock
summary:: A clock that runs without time, for rendering a take offline
categories:: Libraries>reCording
related:: Guides/reCording, Classes/REScorePlayer, Classes/RCSession

DESCRIPTION::
What a song schedules on it (its beats' players, its Routines, a replay) runs when the clock is stepped (link::#-advanceTo::), so that a take renders without a server: the messages the song sends go to an code::RECollectAddr::, timed by this clock, and become a link::Classes/Score::. It keeps the TempoClock interface the reCurrent classes and the streams use. While an item runs, the main thread's clock, beats and seconds are this clock's, as AppClock does through its Scheduler: a Routine resumed then inherits them and code::n.wait:: reschedules it here. Nothing runs until advanceTo is called.

code::RECollectAddr:: is a NetAddr that keeps what is sent to it (code::sendMsg::, code::sendBundle::, the list forms) as code::[seconds, msg, ...]:: with the clock's seconds plus the bundle's latency, instead of sending; code::score(defs):: answers a Score of them, the SynthDefs first.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
argument:: tempo

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: advanceTo
argument:: target
Runs everything due up to that beat, in order, then stands there.
METHOD:: advance
argument:: deltaBeats
METHOD:: beats
METHOD:: seconds
METHOD:: tempo
METHOD:: nextDue
The beat of the next item, nil when nothing is queued.
METHOD:: wakeups
Items run so far.

EXAMPLES::

code::
c = REOfflineClock(tempo: 2);
a = RECollectAddr("127.0.0.1", 57999, c);
s = Server(\offline, a, ServerOptions.new.numOutputBusChannels_(2));
Server.default = s;
RCSession.boot(s, c, oscPort: 32397, initMidi: false);
~song = RCSong(\offline, 1);
~b = ~song.layer(\core).addBeat(\k, [instrument: \default, dur: 0.5, freq: 440, amp: 0.1]);
~p = REScorePlayer(REScore.read(path), ~song);
~p.alignPhase = false;
~p.play(0);
c.advanceTo(64);
a.score([SynthDescLib.global[\default].def]).recordNRT("/tmp/take.osc", "/tmp/take.wav", duration: 32.5, action: { 0.exit });
::
